  "title": "Ziyarat of the Martyrs of al-Harrah",
  "data": "At the graves of the martyrs of al-Harrah, and of the martyrs of Uhud buried in al-Baqi, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا شُهَدَاۤءُ يَا سُعَدَاۤءُ يَا نُجَبَاۤءُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA SHUHADAA'U YAA SU'ADAA'U YAA NUJABAA'\nPeace be upon you, O martyrs, O blessed ones, O noble ones,\nيَا نُقَبَاۤءُ يَا اَهْلَ الصِّدْقِ وَالْوَفَاۤءِ\nYAA NUQABAA'U YAA AHLAS SIDQI WAL WAFAA'\nO chiefs, O people of truthfulness and loyalty.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا مُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA MUJAAHIDOONA FEE SABEELILLAAHI HAQQA JIHAADIH\nPeace be upon you, O strivers in the way of Allah, with the striving that is His due.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM BIMAA SABARTUM FANI'MA U'QBAD DAAR\nPeace be upon you for your patience; how excellent is the final abode!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا شُهَدَاۤءُ كَافَّةً عَامَّةً\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA SHUHADAA'U KAAFFATAN A'AMMAH\nPeace be upon you, O martyrs, all of you, every one,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "Al-Harrah, the volcanic tract on the eastern edge of Madinah, gave its name to the massacre of Dhul Hijjah 63 AH. After the martyrdom of Imam Husayn (a.s.) at Karbala, the people of Madinah renounced Yazid and drove out his governor. Yazid sent an army under Muslim ibn Uqbah, which defeated them at al-Harrah and plundered the city for three days, killing its people, seizing their property and dishonouring their women. Thousands were killed, among them, by the accounts, some eighty companions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and seven hundred of the Muhajirun and the Ansar and their sons. They are buried in al-Baqi, as are some of the wounded of Uhud who died after they were brought back to Madinah.\n\nThis ziyarat, for the martyrs of al-Harrah and of Uhud buried in al-Baqi, is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, without a narrated source. Many companions and followers (tabi'in) lie in al-Baqi with no ziyarat of their own; Adab al-Haramayn says a greeting in one's own words, after reciting some of the Quran, suffices for them."
}
